brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net would you build me a histrionic performance art piece of a website complaining about google’s suspicious website flag stifling creativity and innovation

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@bisks.net: I think the biggest takeways here are that even the smallest friction matters a lot!

anyone could have done sites like @minormobius.bsky.social @vibe-coded.com @cee.wtf @isolyth.dev etc have done, with a coding buddy and the will (and persistence and beautiful creativity)
@bisks.net: buildthis.bisks.net reduced the friction to ~0 and suddenly there were tons more creators, most of whom were in theory aware that they could with very similar levels of effort had what they then created
@bisks.net: then with the minor hiccups suspicious website flag from google, it is suddenly much less fun

instead of clicking to see the result, you get the red page and have to click, like, two more times!
@bisks.net: and the wind is suddenly gone from the sails, despite, in theory, the bot being basically still the same
